    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a high-floor offensive configuration, headlined by the dual-threat speed and power upside of **Corbin Carroll** (79.46) and **Josh Naylor** (78.09). **Corbin Carroll** is our primary target against the left-handed Andrew Abbott; despite a platoon disadvantage, the aggressive top-of-the-order environment and favorable park factors make him an elite start. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (75.99) benefit from optimal lineup placement and advantageous matchups against Spencer Arrighetti and Tomoyuki Sugano, respectively. **Jose Caballero** (73.65) remains a critical anchor for our stolen base strategy, as his dynamic platoon edge against Patrick Corbin provides a significant boost that outweighs his lower spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench was **Kyle Karros** (54.63), who fell just shy of replacing **Max Muncy** (55.89). While **Kyle Karros** shows promise against Jeffrey Springs, the optimizer favored **Max Muncy**\u2019s matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano, trusting the latter\u2019s underlying consistency despite a lukewarm projection. Managers should remain alert to the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Cole Young**, as these assumptions are driving their volatility. While **James Wood** (65.20) carries high expectations due to an elite 0.403 xwOBA, caution is advised as he faces an opponent with an \"Elite Hold\" capability, potentially limiting the stolen base opportunities that are essential for our roster. We continue to prioritize efficiency over chasing home runs, keeping players like **Seiya Suzuki** and **Brice Turang** on the pine due to their difficult matchups against Logan Webb and Cristopher S\u00e1nchez, respectively.",
